Sorry to have been away from this thread for a while; I had a business
trip.

My original questions was this, now using the concepts that developed
in the threads: Of all the games that end with an ascension, in what
percentage of these did the character have the survival final
attribute?  The remaining percentage of games used at least one "oLS.
I don't particularly care whether the surviving character wore an
amulet that wasn't used or never wore an amulet of life-saving.

It seems to me that a two step process would work.

1. Out of all dumplogs, keep those with the line: "Killer: ascended"
2. Out of the dumplogs that passed step 1, keep those with the line:
"You survived" among the final attributes.

The count of those dumplogs passing step 2 divided by the count of
those dumplogs passing step 1 would be the percentage of those
ascensions that did not involve a life-saving event.

I could easily write a script in Python that would perform steps 1 and
2, given a dumplog's URL.  What I don't know how to do is to generate
the URLs of all the dumplogs.

